BPF struct_ops providers resolve their CFI stubs through kallsyms and
require vmlinux BTF.  Without that complete build-time contract their
registration fails during boot even though Kconfig presented the
providers as usable.

Represent these prerequisites with a hidden BPF_STRUCT_OPS capability.
Gate every in-tree runtime provider on it, including HID-BPF, while
leaving ordinary BPF and non-struct_ops consumers available without
KALLSYMS.  Leave the core test-run callback unset when the capability
omits its dummy provider.

Keep existing scheduler dependencies in place so experimental
alternative schedulers retain their independent SCHED_CLASS_EXT
exclusion.

diff --git a/drivers/hid/bpf/Kconfig b/drivers/hid/bpf/Kconfig
